# What the site build does not need.
#
# The deploy runs from the repo root, because fusion/site is a workspace package and
# its dependencies are built from source. That would otherwise upload a great
# deal the build has no use for.
#
# Leading slash matters: `docs/` is a gitignore-style pattern and would also
# match `cortex/docs` and `helix/docs`, which are workspace members. Excluding
# those breaks `bun install` before the build starts.
#
# `fusion/docs/insights` is `@fusion.dev/insights`, a workspace member the site
# depends on, so the folder itself can never be excluded.
#
# So the pattern names the files rather than the folder. The two markdown
# documents left at the top of `fusion/docs/` are generated references, neither
# read by anything on the build path and both repository-internal, which
# `fusion/site/app/helix/tokens.json/route.ts` says of the token reference in as
# many words.
/fusion/docs/*.md

# Build output and scratch, rebuilt on Vercel anyway.
.claude/
.local/
target/
**/.next/
**/.turbo/
**/dist/
**/node_modules/

# Rust, which nothing in this project builds.
Cargo.lock
Cargo.toml
